Q: Subclassing CanvasRenderingContext2D A: <p>Greetings from the future. There’s a similar problem at <a href="https://stackoverflow.com/questions/36299883/how-to-extend-canvasrenderingcontext2d-in-es6-style-scripts-if-possible">How to extend CanvasRenderingContext2D (in ES6-style scripts, if possible)</a> . Here is some code (no coffescript) inspired by the answer at #answer-73676870 :</p>
<pre class="lang-js prettyprint-override"><code>class ContextSub extends CanvasRenderingContext2D {
    constructor(canvas) {
        let object = Object.setPrototypeOf(canvas.getContext('2d'), new.target.prototype);
        return object;
    }
    //  etc
}


let canvas = document.querySelector('canvas#…');
let context = new ContextSub(canvas);
</code></pre>
<p>The <code>Object.setPrototypeOf()</code> method attaches a prototype to an object. Here we’re attaching the prototype of the new ContextSub object (<code>new.target</code>) to the context object from <code>getContext()</code>.</p>
<p>You don’t normally see <code>return</code> in a constructor. However, in this case, we’re returning an alternative object rather than the default one.</p>

Q: JSONParser missing from JDK A: <p>The dependency with JSON parser implementation to be paired with the dependency of <strong>jakarta.json-api</strong>:</p>
<pre class="lang-xml prettyprint-override"><code>&lt;dependency&gt;
    &lt;groupId&gt;org.glassfish&lt;/groupId&gt;
